Tell the shell which link the pointer is over.

Chromium writes the hovered URL into the status bubble at the bottom of the
window. With the frame hidden there is no status bubble, the loop finds no
anchor and the hover is simply dropped, so a shell drawing its own corner
label has nothing to put in it.

Only taken when the shell draws that label; otherwise Chromium's bubble is
still there and still right.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

